And so John came. He baptized people in the wilderness. And he preached to them about baptism and repentance for sins. God forgives them after that.
All the people from the interior of Judea went out to him. All the people from Jerusalem walked, they were with him. When they confessed their sin, John baptized them in the river Jordan.
John wore clothes made of camel's hair. He had a leather belt around his waist. And all he ate was locusts and wild honey.
This is what John used to preach: "After me comes one who is mightier than I. I am not worthy to untie the thong of his sandals."
"We baptize you with water. But he will baptize you with the Holy Spirit." The baptism and temptation of Jesus.
At that time, Jesus came from Nazareth in Galilee. John baptized him in the River Jordan.
Jesus was coming up out of the water. At that moment, he saw the heavens opened, and he saw the Spirit descend on him like a dove.
A voice spoke to him from the sky. It said: "You are my son, and I love you very much. I am pleased with you as you are."
Immediately, the Spirit sent Jesus out into the wilderness.
He was in the wilderness for forty days. There the devil tempted him. The beasts did not harm Jesus. Angels were protecting him. Jesus chooses the first disciples.
After they imprisoned John, Jesus went to Galilee. He preached the good news of God.
"The time has come," he said. "The Kingdom of God is near. Repent of your sins and believe in the Gospel!"
One day, Jesus was walking by the Sea of Galilee. There he saw Simon and his brother Andrew. They were casting a net into the lake. They were fishermen.
"Come, follow Me," Jesus said. "I will make you fishers of men."
Immediately they left their nets and followed him.
Then Jesus walked a little further. And behold, he saw James the son of Zebedee, and his brother John. And they were in a boat repairing their fishing nets.
Immediately he called them. They left their father Zebedee in the boat with the hired men. Then they followed Jesus. Jesus drives out a demon.
Jesus and those with him went to Kafarna. When the Sabbath came, he entered the synagogue. There he began to teach.
People were amazed at his method of teaching. He taught them as if he were someone with authority. He did not speak as if they were the scholars.
At that moment, a man in the synagogue cried out. For he was not himself, but was possessed by an unclean spirit. And he said,
What do you want from us, Jesus of Nazareth? Did you come to destroy us? We know who you are, the holy one of God!
"Be quiet!" Jesus said firmly. "Come out of him!"
The evil spirit violently shook the man. Then it came out of him with a scream.
Everyone was amazed and began to ask each other, "What is this? A new teaching! And with such authority! He even commands the evil spirits, and they obey him!"
News of Jesus spread rapidly throughout Galilee. Jesus heals many people.
Jesus and those who were with him went out of the synagogue. Immediately they went with James and John to the house of Simon and Andrew.
Mother of Simon's wife was lying in bed. She had a fever. They told Jesus about her.
He went to her. He held her hand and helped her up. The free woman was back. Then she started serving them.
That evening, after sunset, they brought to the Lord Jesus all who were sick. They also brought all who were possessed by demons.
Everyone in the city gathered in front of the door.
Jesus healed many of them. They had all kinds of diseases. He also drove out many demons. But he did not let the demons speak, because they knew who he was. Jesus prays in a quiet place.
It was still before dawn and the air was dark. Jesus got up and went out of the house. He walked to a garden where he could be alone. There he prayed to God.
Simon and his friends went to look for Jesus.
When they found him, they called out, "Everyone is looking for you!"
Jesus answered, "Let us go to another town. I want to go to the nearby country. I must preach there too. This is why I came."
Tuna walked throughout Galilee. Preaching in their churches. And casting out demons. Jesus heals a man with a skin disease.
A man who had a skin disease came to Jesus. He knelt down and begged Jesus. He said, "If you are willing to make me 'clean', then it is within your power."
Jesus was filled with profound concern. He reached out and touched the man. "I am willing to do this," he said. "Be clean!"
Immediately the illness departed from him. May God heal him.
Jesus sent him immediately. He warned him severely.
"Don't tell this to anyone," he said. "Go show yourself to the Pasha. Perform the sacrifices that Moses commanded. This will be a witness to the Pasha and to everyone that you are 'clean'."
But the man went out and began to speak directly. He spread the news to everyone. Because Jesus could no longer enter the city openly. He remained outside in deserted places. But the people still came to him from everywhere.
Jesus heals a man who couldn't walk.
Within a few days after this, Jesus entered Capernaum again. The people heard that he had returned home.
The crowd was so large that there was no more room. There wasn't even any space outside the door. And Jesus, he was standing there explaining it to them.
Four of those who came were carrying a man who could not walk.
But they couldn't get him close to Jesus because the crowd was very large. So they made a hole in the roof above Jesus. Then they lowered the man on a stretcher through it.
Jesus saw their faith. He said to the man, "Son, your sins are forgiven."
Some jurists were sitting there. They were thinking,
What is that person talking like that for? He says a bad word, okay! God is the one who forgives sins!
Essa's tuna felt what was on their minds. He said to them, "What do you think is on your minds?"
Is it easier to say to this man, 'Your sins are forgiven'? than to say, 'Rise, take up your bed and walk'?
"We love you. Do you know that the Son of Man has authority on earth to forgive sins?" Then Jesus spoke to the man who could not walk.
"I can tell you," he said, "you can sit down. Take your things and go home."
The man got up and took his mat. Then he walked, with all the people watching him. All the people were amazed. They praised God and said, "We have never seen anything like this!" Jesus chooses Levi.
Again Jesus went out beside the Sea of Galilee. A great crowd came to him. He began to teach them.
