People don't put new wine into old wine skins. If they do, the wine will burst the skins. Then the wine and the skins will both be lost. No, everyone puts new wine into new wine skins." Jesus Lord of the Sabbath.
On a Saturday, Jesus was walking with his disciples in the fields. The disciples began to pick wheat spikes.
The Pharisees said to Jesus, "Look! It is not lawful to do this on the Sabbath. Why then do your disciples do it?"
Answer, "Have you not read what David did? He and his men were hungry. They needed food."
This was at a time when Abiathar was the high priest. David entered the house of God and ate the holy bread. Only the priests were allowed to eat it. And David gave some of it to his men as well.
Jesus said to them, "The Sabbath was made for man, and not man for the Sabbath."
Therefore, the Son of Man is also Lord of the Sabbath."
Healing on the Sabbath.
Again Jesus entered the synagogue. There was a man there whose hand was withered and deformed.
Some Pharisees were trying to find fault with Jesus. They watched him closely. They wanted to see if he would heal a man on the Sabbath day.
Jesus said to the man who had a withered hand: "Stand up in front of everyone."
Then Jesus asked them, "What does the Law say about the Sabbath? Is it to do good or evil? Is it to save life or to kill?" But no one answered him.
Jesus looked around at them with anger. He was very upset because their hearts were hardened. Then He said to the man, "Stretch out your hand." So he stretched it out, and his hand was restored like a completely new hand.
Then the Pharisees went out and began to plot with the Herodians against Jesus, seeking to kill him. The crowds follow Jesus.
Jesus went with his disciples to the Sea of Galilee. A large crowd from Galilee followed him.
People heard about all the things Jesus was doing. And many people came to see him. They came from Judea, Jerusalem, and Idumea. They came from the region east of the Jordan River. And they came from the areas around Tyre and Sidon.
Because of the crowd, Jesus told His disciples to prepare a small boat for Him. This would prevent people from crowding Him.
Jesus healed many people. Because of this, those who were sick used to warm themselves in order to touch him.
When those who had demons saw him, they fell down before him. And the demons cried out, "You are the Son of God!"
Jesus instructed them not to say who he was. Jesus appoints the twelve apostles.
Follow Jesus up the mountain. He called certain persons to come to him, and they came to him.
He appointed twelve of them and called them apostles. From then on, they were with him. And he used to send them out to preach.
They possessed the power to expel demons.
Jesus examined the twelve apostles. Simon was one of them. Jesus named him Peter.
There was James the son of Zebedee, and his brother John. Jesus gave them the name Boanerges. Boanerges means Sons of Thunder.
There was also Andrew, Philip, Bartholomew, Matthew, Thomas, and James the son of Alphaeus. And there was Thaddaeus and Simon the Zealot.
